Sensitive field exposure: Lombok `@Data` auto-generates `toString()`/`equals()`/`hashCode()` that include the plaintext password. Any framework or diagnostic logging of this object (Spring MVC debug logging, `@RestControllerAdvice` handlers, exception dumps, or future `log.info("...{}", request)`) will leak the credential. Exclude the password from `toString()`:

```java
import lombok.ToString;
...
@ToString.Exclude
private String password;
```
(or annotate the class with `@ToString(exclude = "password")`).

